  "_comment": "Hand-written entries not covered by desktop-pkgs.json: KDE/GNOME desktop-environment apps, apps that ship a real Linux binary, plus placeholder Apple/Microsoft entries for apps that don't exist on every OS. `bin` is a per-OS object ({\"linux\": ..., \"windows\": ..., \"macos\": ...}); any key can be omitted, meaning the app doesn't exist on that OS, so is_installed returns false for it there with no extra logic needed. Most Apple/Microsoft entries only have one key (mac-* -> macos, win-* -> windows) since they're single-platform. microsoft-edge/powershell/onedrive-client are the few entries with a real, hand-verified triple across all three OSes -- unverified on actual Windows/macOS hardware, but the names themselves are well-known.",
